# Kept out of the published archive.
#
# This file REPLACES .gitignore for publishing rather than adding to it, so it
# has to restate the build-output patterns as well as its own exclusions.
# Leaving them out ships the Dart build cache — tens of megabytes of .dill.

# Build output and caches, in this package and in the example.
.dart_tool/
build/
coverage/
**/.dart_tool/
**/build/

# `docs/` and `tools/` are named for the repository, where they sit next to the
# same directories in the application this kit came from. Pub's layout
# convention is the singular `doc/` and `tool/`, and it fails a publish over the
# difference — so the directories keep their names here and simply do not ship.
# Neither is of any use to a consumer: one documents releasing this package, the
# other runs its checks.
#
# README links into docs/ still resolve, because pub.dev rewrites relative links
# against the `repository:` field in pubspec.yaml.
docs/
tools/

# CI configuration is repository infrastructure, not part of the package.
.github/

# The gallery ships as source — it is the package's example — but its platform
# scaffolding is generated and of no interest to anyone reading it.
example/linux/
example/.metadata

# Editor and tooling leftovers.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log
